 "short_name": "Witzenberg",
 "_doc": "Witzenberg LM (Ceres). Two layouts of the same bill: older (letters doubled in headings, columns BASIC/VAT/AMOUNT, space-thousands) and newer (columns VAT/CHARGE(5 dp)/AMOUNT); both have the account row (prefix + account, date of account, site, erf ...), METER READINGS (E/K rows) and TRANSACTION DETAILS where AMOUNT is VAT-INCLUSIVE and VAT is printed per line. Electricity: 'Electricity DTL4/DTL5/DTL6' = TOU registers, mapped peak/standard/off-peak because their ex-VAT rate per kWh is consistently highest/middle/lowest on all 9 bills (about 3.0/2.2/1.45 R/kWh low season); 'KVA DTL' = demand kVA, its printed fixed BASIC/CHARGE part goes to other_r and the rest to demand_r; 'KVA CAPA' = capacity charge -> nmd_r, nmd_kva = the constant second K register. Fingerprint: municipal VAT number (+ any of its B.T.W. label / name / town). IDENTITY: wz_elec_ex_by_vat_r = electricity VAT x (1/0.15) vs total_ex_vat_r: <=R0.05 on 8/9, R0.12 on 1 (five lines' VAT rounding, each line within R0.04); side check: electricity + water/sewer/refuse VAT = printed TOTAL VAT on 8/8 bills that print it. Checked on 9 bills (two files are duplicates of one month).",
